      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Reviews work against the plan between tasks and reports issues by severity, with critical issues blocking progress."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_finishing_a_development_branch",
      "label": "finishing-a-development-branch skill",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Verifies tests when tasks complete, then presents merge/PR/keep/discard options and cleans up the worktree."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_diagnosing_superpowers",
      "label": "diagnosing-superpowers skill",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Reads the session transcript and reports what happened with line-level evidence when a session misbehaves, and can package a scrubbed bundle for a bug report."
    },
    {
      "id": "readme_using_superpowers",
      "label": "using-superpowers bootstrap skill",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\README.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Injects the bootstrap that makes the skills system active at session start; without it (e.g. Hermes sessions compacted past the first turn, or missing hooks) skills stop triggering."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_readme_kimi_plugin_manifest",
      "label": "Kimi Code plugin manifest (.kimi-plugin/plugin.json)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\README.kimi.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The manifest points Kimi Code at the existing skills/ directory, loads using-superpowers at session start via sessionStart.skill, and provides Kimi-specific tool mapping via skillInstructions; skills are read in place with no copies, symlinks, hooks or extra runtime dependencies."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_readme_kimi_tool_mapping",
      "label": "Kimi Code tool mapping (AskUserQuestion, TodoList, Agent, Skill, Read/Write/Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, FetchURL, WebSearch)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\README.kimi.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Skills describe actions instead of hard-coding one runtime's tool names, so on Kimi Code the abstract actions resolve to Kimi's native tool names."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_readme_opencode_bootstrap_injection",
      "label": "OpenCode bootstrap injection (controller session, compaction handling)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\README.opencode.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Controller sessions receive the using-superpowers bootstrap in transient model context; delegated child sessions keep native skills but not the controller bootstrap; when V2 compaction removes all user messages the plugin appends a transient bootstrap after the checkpoint so skills keep triggering in long sessions."
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_readme_opencode_tool_mapping",
      "label": "OpenCode V1/V2 tool mapping (task->subagent, apply_patch->patch, bash->shell, todo dropped in V2)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\README.opencode.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Skills speak in actions rather than naming any one runtime's tools, so the bootstrap maps them to the tools each OpenCode flavor actually exposes; V2 renamed task to subagent, apply_patch to patch, bash to shell, and dropped the todo tool entirely."
    }
  ],
